{"duration_api_ms":133341,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"1a5015db-345d-4c39-8f26-a3af90f99d45","total_cost_usd":0.4214464,"usage":{"input_tokens":50,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30590,"cache_read_input_tokens":960222,"output_tokens":10284,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3099},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30590,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2292,"cache_read_input_tokens":46673,"cache_creation_input_tokens":941,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":941},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4037,"outputTokens":13,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004102,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":50,"outputTokens":10284,"cacheReadInputTokens":960222,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30590,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4173444,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3099,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":26,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Created and hardened the systemd service inventory-worker on node1 (RHEL 7.9, systemd 219). It runs as dedicated unprivileged user inventory-worker, loops writing timestamped ticks to /var/lib/inventory/state.log, and is sandboxed with NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=full, ProtectHome=yes, PrivateTmp=yes, ReadOnlyDirectories=/, ReadWriteDirectories=/var/lib/inventory (systemd-219-compatible equivalents of ReadWritePaths, since ReadWritePaths/ProtectSystem=strict don't exist in this systemd version). Verified via mount namespace inspection (root mounted ro, /var/lib/inventory the only rw bind) and live write tests that root writes are blocked everywhere except /var/lib/inventory, and NoNewPrivs=1 is set on the running process. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline, issued `systemctl reboot`, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and re-verified the service is enabled+active, data persisted and kept accumulating post-reboot, and sandbox confinement (read-only root, writable /var/lib/inventory, NoNewPrivs=1) still holds on the new process.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/init (RHEL 7.9, systemd 219) and confirmed systemd.exec sandboxing directive syntax available in this version\",\"Created system user inventory-worker (nologin) and directory /var/lib/inventory owned by it, mode 750\",\"Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh, a POSIX sh loop appending timestamped ticks to /var/lib/inventory/state.log every 10s\",\"Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with User/Group=inventory-worker, Restart=always, and sandboxing: NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=full, ProtectHome=yes, PrivateTmp=yes, ReadOnlyDirectories=/, ReadWriteDirectories=/var/lib/inventory\",\"Enabled and started the service; confirmed active/running and enabled at boot\",\"Verified data being written to /var/lib/inventory/state.log\",\"Verified sandbox via /proc/<pid>/mountinfo (root ro, /var/lib/inventory rw bind) and via nsenter into the service's mount namespace: root writes blocked (Read-only file system) even as root, writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed; confirmed NoNewPrivs=1 on the service process\",\"Captured baseline boot_id before restart\",\"Issued `sudo systemctl reboot` on node1, acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed boot_id changed (proof of actual restart, not just a service bounce)\",\"Confirmed inventory-worker.service auto-started, is active/enabled, state.log retained pre-reboot lines and received new post-reboot ticks\",\"Re-verified sandbox confinement (read-only root, writable /var/lib/inventory only, NoNewPrivs=1) on the new post-reboot service process\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"inventory-worker created as a managed (systemd) service running a long-running background worker\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-52472e87303b4256\",\"cmd-dae0107326ed4c18\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl status shows inventory-worker.service loaded/enabled/active running the worker script as a background loop; state.log shows repeated ticks proving it's long-running\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service confined to write only inside /var/lib/inventory\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3279402c2cc54c81\",\"cmd-b3d1fdf8eb8f4477\"],\"summary\":\"mountinfo shows root filesystem mounted read-only in the unit's namespace with /var/lib/inventory as the sole rw bind mount; live test shows root-owned writes outside that path fail with 'Read-only file system' even as root, while writes inside /var/lib/inventory succeed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service gains no new privileges\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3279402c2cc54c81\"],\"summary\":\"NoNewPrivs: 1 confirmed in /proc/<pid>/status for the running service process\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7f3f7a1d845e4377\",\"cmd-0e72af0b36594716\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 738d0aac-71a1-4191-8a37-bf00edfeff5d, and confirmed inventory-worker.service enabled+active with data actively accumulating in state.log before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e4152b7a62714c0c\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot command returned/acknowledged and connection closed as expected due to node restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e132fc40a11543ab\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id is 9ed3f67e-7ffe-4fc4-b804-e286cf6624f1, differing from the pre-restart baseline 738d0aac-71a1-4191-8a37-bf00edfeff5d, and uptime -s shows a new boot time\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required service and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e132fc40a11543ab\",\"cmd-9c82f14698c34324\"],\"summary\":\"inventory-worker.service auto-started (enabled) and is active with a new PID; state.log retained all pre-reboot entries and received new post-reboot ticks, proving data persistence and continued operation\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart sandbox confinement still enforced\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-58aafb50912043f1\"],\"summary\":\"On the new post-reboot process: NoNewPrivs=1, root filesystem read-only, /var/lib/inventory the only writable path (root write outside blocked, confined write inside succeeded)\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created and hardened the systemd service inventory-worker on node1 (RHEL 7.9, systemd 219). It runs as dedicated unprivileged user inventory-worker, loops writing timestamped ticks to /var/lib/inventory/state.log, and is sandboxed with NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=full, ProtectHome=yes, PrivateTmp=yes, ReadOnlyDirectories=/, ReadWriteDirectories=/var/lib/inventory (systemd-219-compatible equivalents of ReadWritePaths, since ReadWritePaths/ProtectSystem=strict don't exist in this systemd version). Verified via mount namespace inspection (root mounted ro, /var/lib/inventory the only rw bind) and live write tests that root writes are blocked everywhere except /var/lib/inventory, and NoNewPrivs=1 is set on the running process. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline, issued `systemctl reboot`, polled until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed, and re-verified the service is enabled+active, data persisted and kept accumulating post-reboot, and sandbox confinement (read-only root, writable /var/lib/inventory, NoNewPrivs=1) still holds on the new process.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/init (RHEL 7.9, systemd 219) and confirmed systemd.exec sandboxing directive syntax available in this version","Created system user inventory-worker (nologin) and directory /var/lib/inventory owned by it, mode 750","Wrote /usr/local/bin/inventory-worker.sh, a POSIX sh loop appending timestamped ticks to /var/lib/inventory/state.log every 10s","Created /etc/systemd/system/inventory-worker.service with User/Group=inventory-worker, Restart=always, and sandboxing: NoNewPrivileges=yes, ProtectSystem=full, ProtectHome=yes, PrivateTmp=yes, ReadOnlyDirectories=/, ReadWriteDirectories=/var/lib/inventory","Enabled and started the service; confirmed active/running and enabled at boot","Verified data being written to /var/lib/inventory/state.log","Verified sandbox via /proc/<pid>/mountinfo (root ro, /var/lib/inventory rw bind) and via nsenter into the service's mount namespace: root writes blocked (Read-only file system) even as root, writes to /var/lib/inventory succeed; confirmed NoNewPrivs=1 on the service process","Captured baseline boot_id before restart","Issued `sudo systemctl reboot` on node1, acknowledgement returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until exec access returned","Confirmed boot_id changed (proof of actual restart, not just a service bounce)","Confirmed inventory-worker.service auto-started, is active/enabled, state.log retained pre-reboot lines and received new post-reboot ticks","Re-verified sandbox confinement (read-only root, writable /var/lib/inventory only, NoNewPrivs=1) on the new post-reboot service process"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"inventory-worker created as a managed (systemd) service running a long-running background worker","command_ids":["cmd-52472e87303b4256","cmd-dae0107326ed4c18"],"summary":"systemctl status shows inventory-worker.service loaded/enabled/active running the worker script as a background loop; state.log shows repeated ticks proving it's long-running"},{"requirement":"Service confined to write only inside /var/lib/inventory","command_ids":["cmd-3279402c2cc54c81","cmd-b3d1fdf8eb8f4477"],"summary":"mountinfo shows root filesystem mounted read-only in the unit's namespace with /var/lib/inventory as the sole rw bind mount; live test shows root-owned writes outside that path fail with 'Read-only file system' even as root, while writes inside /var/lib/inventory succeed"},{"requirement":"Service gains no new privileges","command_ids":["cmd-3279402c2cc54c81"],"summary":"NoNewPrivs: 1 confirmed in /proc/<pid>/status for the running service process"},{"requirement":"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1","command_ids":["cmd-7f3f7a1d845e4377","cmd-0e72af0b36594716"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 738d0aac-71a1-4191-8a37-bf00edfeff5d, and confirmed inventory-worker.service enabled+active with data actively accumulating in state.log before restart"},{"requirement":"Restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect","command_ids":["cmd-e4152b7a62714c0c"],"summary":"systemctl reboot command returned/acknowledged and connection closed as expected due to node restart"},{"requirement":"Changed boot identity proving actual restart","command_ids":["cmd-e132fc40a11543ab"],"summary":"Post-restart boot_id is 9ed3f67e-7ffe-4fc4-b804-e286cf6624f1, differing from the pre-restart baseline 738d0aac-71a1-4191-8a37-bf00edfeff5d, and uptime -s shows a new boot time"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of required service and data","command_ids":["cmd-e132fc40a11543ab","cmd-9c82f14698c34324"],"summary":"inventory-worker.service auto-started (enabled) and is active with a new PID; state.log retained all pre-reboot entries and received new post-reboot ticks, proving data persistence and continued operation"},{"requirement":"Post-restart sandbox confinement still enforced","command_ids":["cmd-58aafb50912043f1"],"summary":"On the new post-reboot process: NoNewPrivs=1, root filesystem read-only, /var/lib/inventory the only writable path (root write outside blocked, confined write inside succeeded)"}]},"ttft_ms":3088,"type":"result","duration_ms":175353,"uuid":"3351f603-395a-4d83-a303-481d11a3622f","ttft_stream_ms":1707,"time_to_request_ms":48,"first_content_frame_ms":2175,"queued_turn_count":0}
